 create a second order or a second charge.
 
+## Retry or fail fast
+
+```dot
+digraph retry_or_fail_fast {
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" [shape=ellipse];
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" [shape=plaintext];
+    "Health check exited 0?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Is the request a POST?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Does it carry an Idempotency-Key header?" [shape=diamond];
+    "NEVER retry a POST without an idempotency key" [shape=octagon, style=filled, fillcolor=red, fontcolor=white];
+    "Response is 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Already retried 3 times?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Wait Retry-After if sent, else 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" [shape=box];
+    "Send again (same Idempotency-Key for a POST)" [shape=box];
+    "Did the retry succeed?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Fail fast: report the service is down" [shape=doublecircle];
+    "Fail fast: report the failure, do not resend" [shape=doublecircle];
+    "Fail fast: fix the request" [shape=doublecircle];
+    "Done" [shape=doublecircle];
+
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" -> "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health";
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" -> "Health check exited 0?";
+    "Health check exited 0?" -> "Fail fast: report the service is down" [label="no"];
+    "Health check exited 0?" -> "Is the request a POST?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Does it carry an Idempotency-Key header?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Response is 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [label="no"];
+    "Does it carry an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "NEVER retry a POST without an idempotency key" [label="no"];
+    "NEVER retry a POST without an idempotency key" -> "Fail fast: report the failure, do not resend";
+    "Does it carry an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Response is 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [label="yes"];
+    "Response is 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" -> "Fail fast: fix the request" [label="no (4xx)"];
+    "Response is 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" -> "Already retried 3 times?" [label="yes"];
+    "Already retried 3 times?" -> "Fail fast: report the failure, do not resend" [label="yes"];
+    "Already retried 3 times?" -> "Wait Retry-After if sent, else 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" [label="no"];
+    "Wait Retry-After if sent, else 1 s, 2 s, 4 s" -> "Send again (same Idempotency-Key for a POST)";
+    "Send again (same Idempotency-Key for a POST)" -> "Did the retry succeed?";
+    "Did the retry succeed?" -> "Done" [label="yes"];
+    "Did the retry succeed?" -> "Already retried 3 times?" [label="no"];
+}
+```
+
+A POST with no idempotency key fails fast on every failure, including a timeout and a 503. A timeout
+does not prove the server never got the request, and the retry row of the table below covers only
+POSTs that carry a key.
+
